From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:55:39 -0500
Subject: feat: a Space's session shows as a line in its colour (S-477)

Spaces can share a named session since 0.4.0 beta 18, and the cookie
badge said only that a Space had a session of its own (GitHub issue 99).
Each named session now has a colour of its own, from six, kept as
sessions are added. In the open sidebar a line in that colour runs
under the chips of a session's Spaces, one line across neighbours, and
a faint line joins them across the Spaces in between; a second session
whose Spaces cross the first's runs one row lower. The owner chose this
from rendered options on 2026-11-13. In the rail, and wherever a
Space's name is shown (its title row, menus, the command bar, page
info, Settings and the archive page), a disc in the session's colour
takes the cookie's place. Each colour has a shade for light grounds and
one for dark, at least 3:1 against the sidebar's tints (sessions S32).

Why: GitHub issue 99, and the owner's choice of the line with a faint
bridge.
Removable when: never; Stedding's own Spaces.
